WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.335
 Robert and Jarred,
congratulations.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.238
You boys have made it into
the final round of this Greek

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.340
mythology inspired competition.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.041
Now when you came here,
we had you make signature

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.176
blades in your signature style.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.778
That's not going
to happen at home.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.282
Instead, you'll be making this
weapon from Greek mythology--

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.420
the sword of Perseus.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:22.822
 All right.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.290
 And we'll see
you in four days.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:24.823
 Good luck.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.026
 Good luck.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.165
 Go get it.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.900
Hurry.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.736
She's a camera hog right there.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.204
So it's day 1.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.040 line:0%
I'm getting ready to start
making the sword of Perseus.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.608
I've never made a sword before.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.678
And now the first one I'm
making is a sword from a god

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.080
basically.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.016
So I'm going to have to
do my best to please the--

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.051
the Greek gods.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:53.820
I'm going with the 80CRV2.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:54.953
It's a good steel.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:55.855
It's tough.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.557
It holds a good edge.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:01.694
My main goal today is to get
this thing forged to shape.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.731
For me, the most difficult
part of forging the sword

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.867
is getting the curves and
the hourglass shape to it.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.735
I'm already getting kind
of thin in the belly

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.839
up here where I need it.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.675
So I'm kind of trying
to avoid a pattern

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.042
to get the blade too thin.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.577
It's taking a little
longer than I--

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:19.712
I'm wanting.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.847 line:0%
But it's, uh--
it's still going--

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.050 line:7%
going good.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.485 line:7%
ROBERT: It's day 1.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.687
I'm back in my home forge
in Middleburgh, New York.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.556
I'm getting ready to start
on the sword of Perseus.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.259
It's going to be a tricky
sword to forge out, for sure.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.628
I'm going to try to make
my blade out of Damascus.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.764
I've got 1084.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.300
I've got 15 and 20.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.470
I want to do a twisted
Damascus and then

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:50.844
cut that in half and sandwich
it around some solid 1084.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.947
And when I grind
down my edge profile,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.716
the edge will show the
1084 when it's etched.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:59.418
And I think it will really,
really look pretty neat.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.722
The only time I have ever
done twisted Damascus

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.257
was with two people.

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:07.660
And we'll see how this goes
doing it with one person.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.962
No, there's no way.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.330
I'm not even going to
bother with twisting.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:15.201
I'm just going to go for
a random pattern Damascus,

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.770
start working this billet
and cut it, restack

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.173
it, and forge weld again.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.141
JARRED: Go get it.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:29.615
Today, I'd like to get the
blade profiled a little better,

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:33.486
and heat treat it, and
start working on the guard.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.354
So I'm getting
ready to quench it.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.590
And as I heat the sword
up for the quench--

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.959
I have never done one this
big, especially in my forge

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:40.826
like this.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.194
It's a lot smaller.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.562
So I'm going to have to
kind of go back and forth

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.532
and move it in and out
and get an even heat.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:53.673
I barely got the
whole edge in there.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.241
Yeah, that's good.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.141
I'll take it.

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:57.944
The heat treat's done.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.213
I'm going to start
working on the guard.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.281
I'm going to use a Damascus,
just because I want to do

00:03:02.347 --> 00:03:03.816
something a little different.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.318
Here we go.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.988 line:0%
And I wanted to basically
make things harder on myself.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.122 line:7%
ROBERT: It's day 2.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.291
I got my billet
with my 1084 core.

00:03:12.357 --> 00:03:14.460
And we're heading in the forge.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:17.796
The big thing today is going
to be profiling my blade,

00:03:17.896 --> 00:03:19.699
getting everything forged out.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.967
I need to keep on schedule.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:24.671
And I need to get
the heat treat today.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.839
I'm moving a ton of steel.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.906
I'm going from the press.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.741
I'm going to the anvil.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.876
And then bam--

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:31.678
[beep]

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.579
My press is down.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.381
It is going to put me
really, really behind.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.785
I don't know what
I'm going to do.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.487
[groans] Yeah, I got nothing.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.722
It's all arm from here on out.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:45.491
[hammering]

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.527
The tang took a bit of
time to get drawn out.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:52.365
And not having that press
is costing me precious time.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.967
It's going to be a
fight to the finish.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.537
 It's the last day.

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:01.306
And we got to get this
thing finished up.

00:04:01.406 --> 00:04:03.309
I'm planning on starting
off with the guard,

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.577
and getting that
thing done, and then

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:11.250
starting working on that disk
pommel and then the handle.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.418
The pommel's attached now.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.387
And the horseshoe
guards are attached.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:19.259
I got to fit the wood
basically in between the two.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:22.060
I wish I would've left the
pommel off and done the wood

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:24.163
first and then welded it on.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:25.731
But it's too late.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.067
And I've just got to kind of
squeeze the stuff in there.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.035
It feels good to me.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.402
It's-- it's light.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.304
And it feels pretty balanced.

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:34.674
I feel good about my sword.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.942
It's a home run.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.377
Hopefully, it's enough to
where I can win the game.

00:04:38.443 --> 00:04:40.546
Girls, what do y'all
think of daddy's sword?

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.548
 It will kill.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.417
 It will kill.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.951
 You got to say it louder.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.853
 It will kill!

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.256
[laughs]

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.491 line:7%
ROBERT: It's the start of day 4.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:57.930
Yesterday, the heat
treat came out perfect.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.131
Yes.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.601
But I got a mountain
of work to do.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:02.835
I'm exhausted.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.704
My back is killing me.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.972
My arm is sore.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:09.909
And I'm really just wishing
that my press was working.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.177
I'm behind schedule.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.012
And I got a lot of
make-up to do today.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:14.513
The handle assembly went great.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.148
And I've got my pins in.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.217
But it's a heavy sword.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:21.153
So the rest of my
time is going to be

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:24.357
hogging some more material off.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:28.494
My arms feel like they're
about ready to fall off.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.663
The pattern looks amazing.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.331
My only regret is
that I couldn't

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:35.500
get more weight off of it.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:40.206
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.841
Now, in Greek mythology,
Perseus used his sword

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:45.310
to decapitate Medusa and
remove her head from her body

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:46.612
to use it as a weapon.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.413
To that end, I will
take your weapon.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.316
And it will help me
deliver some killing

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.886
slashes and blows to liberate
her head from her body.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.887
Robert, you're up first.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:55.588
You ready for this?

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:56.888
 Yes, sir.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:06:00.960
[dramatic music]

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:32.024
 All right, Robert, let's
talk about your sword here.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:36.763
I like the design that you
have of Damascus in there.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.031
But it's so heavy.

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.732
It's about five
pounds over here.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:43.102
But the thing is it's
so forward heavy.

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:44.236
Most of the weight's up here.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.038
When I'm lifting
this, I can feel

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.640
all the stress right there.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:52.010
This is supposed to be meant to
be a single-handed use weapon.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.981
Now, your edge is plenty sharp.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.882
It was easy to thrust and cut.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:07:01.453
And it will kill.

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:02.522
All right, Jarred, your turn.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.322
Are you ready, sir?

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.390
 Yes, sir.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:08.528
[dramatic music]

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:33.518
 All right, Jarred, first up,
you nailed the balance on this.

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:35.087
It's a one-handed sword.

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.489
And it's about three pounds
lighter than your opponent's.

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:40.860
Your edge is razor sharp.

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:42.594
Every slash is deep.

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:44.796
The thrust, no issues at all.

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:50.069
And most importantly,
sir, it will kill.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.404
JAY: All right, bladesmiths,
we took Medusa's head

00:07:52.504 --> 00:07:53.705
during the kill test.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.308
Now the Kraken's
turned to stone.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:57.009
So what I'm going to
do is take your swords

00:07:57.109 --> 00:08:01.313
and beat them mercilessly
into these stone Kraken heads.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.382
It's going to be brutal.

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:05.318
And, Rob, you're up first.

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:06.418
How are you feeling?

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:08.420
 A little nervous,
but I'm ready.

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:13.025
[dramatic music]

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.071
 Are you OK?

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.474
 Yeah, it bounced off
the glove, didn't cut me.

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:31.910
 Well, that's that.

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.178
My blade breaks.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.613
My heart breaks.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:38.450
But I am just so glad
that it didn't hurt Jay.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.654
 Well, a little bit
of a problem here, Rob.

00:08:41.721 --> 00:08:43.756
On the tang, you can
see a black spot.

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.757
So that means you had a
stress fracture there.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:47.993
And with the weight
of this sword

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.129
hitting those stone
Kraken skulls,

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:53.065
it was enough to allow that
stress fracture to just

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.599
continue all the way across.

00:08:54.699 --> 00:08:59.471
So the good part is
that your edge held up--

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:01.040
so good job on the Damascus.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.777
But it's kind of hard to swing
a sword without a handle on it.

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:08.380
WIL: Jarred, your blade still
has to survive four strikes.

00:09:08.446 --> 00:09:10.081
Jay, let's get crack-a-lacking.

00:09:10.148 --> 00:09:14.020
[rock music]

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:33.038
Jarred, your blade survived.

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:36.241
Robert, unfortunately, your
blade cannot continue to be

00:09:36.308 --> 00:09:37.409
tested in this competition.

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:38.677
And for that reason,
I have to ask

00:09:38.743 --> 00:09:40.212
you to please leave the forge.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:41.547
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:41.613 --> 00:09:44.450
You killed the Medusa, though.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:45.884
ROBERT: It really
sucks that it broke.

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:49.654
But this whole experience
has been great.

00:09:49.754 --> 00:09:52.057
And I'm just going to
keep moving forward.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:55.061
I'm just going to keep
getting better at what I do.

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:56.061
It's a heartbreaker.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:57.997
But I'm really
proud of what I did.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.469
 Jarred, congratulations.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:05.271
The strength of your
weapon has ensured

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:08.174
that you are the Forged in
Fire champion leaving this

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.875
forge with a check for $10,000.

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:10.709
Good job, brother.
[applause]

00:10:10.809 --> 00:10:12.011
 Awesome.
Thank you.

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:14.246
Thank you.

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:15.447
 How you feeling right now?

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:16.514
 Good.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:17.282
 How about a
smile or something?

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:18.717
 Yeah.

00:10:18.817 --> 00:10:20.752
 All right, come on over
and shake our hands, brother.

00:10:20.852 --> 00:10:21.921
- Thank you.
- Good job, man.

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:23.456
Good job.

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:24.923
JARRED: I am the new
Forged in Fire champion.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:27.192
That's something I
never thought I'd say.

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.895
I can't wait to get home,
give my daughters the news,

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:33.732
and take the $10,000 and take my
family on a vacation somewhere.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:37.703
[symphonic metal music]

